v {xschem version=3.4.8RC file_version=1.3}
G {}
K {type=primitive
format="@name @pinlist @symname"
spectre_format="@name ( @pinlist ) @symname"
template="name=x1"
}
V {}
S {}
F {}
E {}
* Pin geometry is deliberately identical to devices/ind.sym (p1 at 0,-30 and
* p2 at 0,+30) so this symbol can replace an ideal inductor in place, with no
* rewiring. The body netlists as a primitive subcircuit call, so the actual
* definition comes from whichever LSHUNT_OUT_model.lib section is selected by the
* LVS_MODELS block in lna_core_parts.sch (ideal / rl / snp2le / lvsrm / lvssc).
L 4 0 22.5 0 30 {}
L 4 0 -30 0 -22.5 {}
B 5 -2.5 -32.5 2.5 -27.5 {name=p1 dir=inout propag=1 pinnumber=1}
B 5 -2.5 27.5 2.5 32.5 {name=p2 dir=inout propag=0 pinnumber=2}
P 4 5 -17.5 -22.5 17.5 -22.5 17.5 22.5 -17.5 22.5 -17.5 -22.5 {}
T {@#0:pinnumber} -10 -27.5 0 1 0.2 0.2 {layer=13}
T {@#1:pinnumber} -10 17.5 0 1 0.2 0.2 {layer=13}
T {@#0:net_name} 5 -42.5 0 0 0.15 0.15 {layer=15 hide=instance}
T {@#1:net_name} 5 32.5 0 0 0.15 0.15 {layer=15 hide=instance}
T {@symname} 22.5 -6.25 0 0 0.2 0.2 {}
T {@name} 22.5 -18.75 0 0 0.2 0.2 {}
